{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/678344-ontological-and-metaphysical-questions-of-demonic-inheritance","id":678344,"title":"Ontological and metaphysical questions of Demonic Inheritance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-25T17:52:36-07:00","id":678344,"title":"Ontological and metaphysical questions of Demonic Inheritance","content":"So, someone can become Offspring by their parental relationship being integrated by a Demon (such as the Demon taking a parent in a Soul Pact, or patching in Parent of X into their Cover). Reality changes so that this was always the case.<br /> <br /> Now, how would the following cases be handled?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A Demon takes over <i>both</i> parental attachments, either through Patch or Soul Pact. Does the child become Fractal (as both of their parents are Demons, albeit the <i>same</i> Demon). And how would <i>that</i> be resolved, since either a single individual is both their parents, or one of their parents is only in existence at one time.</li> <li>A Demon assumes the role of John, son of James (Patch or Soul Pact). Said Demon later claims a Soul Pact on Jeremiah, James's father. Is the Demon their own grandpa now, and how does this affect James?</li> <li>A Demon patches in the fatherhood of child X. They then trade this bit of Cover to another Demon. Can that other Demon integrate the fatherhood of child X into a female Cover?</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T22:34:45-07:00","id":679690,"title":"","content":"I'd say that all three are huge Compromise risks.<br /> <br /> 1) Not necessarily a compromise if the Demon puts in the work, and I would say that technically, you are correct (the best kind of correct). The person would probably be Fractal.<br /> <br /> 2) Being your own grandpa would seriously strain things, and I'd rule it a compromise. Jame could reasonably become an Offspring.<br /> <br /> 3) This is tricky. If the patch gives &quot;fatherhood,&quot; then there's gonna be a problem. If the patch only passed over &quot;parenthood,&quot; incidental to gender, then there's less conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T05:04:25-07:00","id":679844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/678344-ontological-and-metaphysical-questions-of-demonic-inheritance?p=679690#post679690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that all three are huge Compromise risks.</div> </div> </div> </div>No doubt. I'm just wondering what contortions reality would have to go through to resolve these.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/678344-ontological-and-metaphysical-questions-of-demonic-inheritance?p=679690#post679690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) This is tricky. If the patch gives &quot;fatherhood,&quot; then there's gonna be a problem. If the patch only passed over &quot;parenthood,&quot; incidental to gender, then there's less conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there is still a problem in that even &quot;parenthood&quot; patched into a female cover makes said Demon the mother, but there is still the <i>actual</i> mother out there, given the hypothetical 2 mothers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}